---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import SiteHeader from "../components/SiteHeader.astro";
import SiteFooter from "../components/SiteFooter.astro";

// The website's privacy policy: the "Get notified" form, analytics and hosting. The app has its
// own policy at after.12f.dk/privacy. What the form must disclose: 12fdk/after-stories#271.
// When anything here changes, change the date.
const updated = "3 October 2026";
---

<Base
  title="Privacy policy — After Stories"
  description="What after-stories.com collects when you sign up to hear about the launch, why, where it's kept and how to have it removed."
>
  <SiteHeader notifyHref="/#notify" />

  <main class="wrap policy">
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated {updated}. This covers the website after-stories.com. The app has its own <a href="https://after.12f.dk/privacy">privacy policy</a>.</p>

    <section>
      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>After Stories is made by <strong>12f ApS</strong>, Denmark, the data controller for this website. Questions about your data: <a href="mailto:support@12f.dk">support@12f.dk</a>.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Getting notified when we launch</h2>
      <p>If you fill in the “Get an email when we launch” form, we collect:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>your <strong>name</strong> and <strong>email address</strong>;</li>
        <li>the <strong>page</strong> you signed up from, so we can see which kind of event brought you here.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We use them to send you <strong>one email to confirm your address</strong>, and once you've confirmed, <strong>one email when After Stories is in the App Store</strong>. Nothing else. If you never confirm, you never get the launch email. We don't sell or share your details, and we don't add you to any other list.</p>
      <p>We do this because you asked us to (your consent, GDPR article 6(1)(a)). You can withdraw it at any time.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Where it's kept, and for how long</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Your sign-up is stored on <strong>our own server in the EU</strong>, in a table no visitor can read.</li>
        <li>The confirmation email is sent through <strong>Brevo</strong>, an email service based in the EU.</li>
        <li>We keep your sign-up for <strong>at most one year</strong>, then delete it.</li>
        <li>Like any web server, ours keeps a <strong>request log</strong>, including your IP address, for a short period, to keep the service running and stop abuse.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Being removed</h2>
      <p>Email <a href="mailto:support@12f.dk">support@12f.dk</a> from the address you signed up with, and we'll delete your sign-up.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Visiting the website</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>The site is hosted on <strong>GitHub Pages</strong>. GitHub processes your IP address to deliver the pages; see <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub's privacy statement</a>.</li>
        <li>We count visits with <strong>Umami</strong>, which we run ourselves. It sets no cookies and doesn't store your IP address or anything that identifies you.</li>
        <li>The fonts are served from this site, not from a font service.</li>
        <li>Your choice of light or dark theme is remembered in your own browser and never sent to us.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>You have the right to see the data we hold about you, to have it corrected or deleted, to take it with you, and to object. Write to <a href="mailto:support@12f.dk">support@12f.dk</a>. You can also complain to the Danish Data Protection Agency, <a href="https://www.datatilsynet.dk">datatilsynet.dk</a>.</p>
    </section>
  </main>

  <SiteFooter />
</Base>

<style>
  .policy {
    max-width: 720px;
    padding-top: 48px;
    padding-bottom: 96px;
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: var(--step-3);
  }

  .updated {
    margin-top: 16px;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  section {
    margin-top: 48px;
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: var(--step-2);
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }

  p + p,
  ul + p,
  p + ul {
    margin-top: 12px;
  }

  ul {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 1.2em;
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  p,
  li {
    max-width: 64ch;
  }

  a {
    color: var(--accent-ink);
  }
</style>
